{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויהי ככלה</b> — when the locust has finished eating the grass of the land, we shall die of famine. The sense of כלה is on account of גז [shearing], like ירד כמטר על גז (Judges 5:4), which is an expression of shearing." "<b>HaShem, forgive now</b> — now, the iniquity of Jacob." "<b>And the word יקום</b> — is among the intransitive verbs [lit. those that stand by themselves], and not among the transitive ones [lit. those that go out upon another]. And the sense: who will stand and who will be able to rise before this trouble, and who will serve on account of another? And thus is מי יקום כי קטן הוא — who will bear this evil, for he is small [i.e., unable to withstand it]."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra's explanation connects כלה to גז by interpreting both as references to cutting/consuming, citing Judges 5:4 (ירד כמטר על גז). The parenthetical verse reference is added for clarity since Ibn Ezra quotes the phrase but does not cite it explicitly.", 2 "The second sentence is compressed and its syntax is strained; rendered hyper-literally. The phrase מסבול זאת הרעה likely means 'from bearing this evil,' but the connective logic between the two Scriptural examples (Amos 7:2 and Amos 7:5) is left implicit as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:29.494883932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}